# DO NOT PUSH CHANGES OF THIS FILE TO opentelemetry/opentelemetry-demo
# PLACE YOUR .env ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES OVERRIDES IN THIS FILE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared with sentinel-rag: this app's own astronomy-db (Postgres) and valkey-cart (Redis) are
# below any real resource threshold (80M / 20M memory limits, see compose.yaml), so rather than
# run a second Postgres and a second Redis container next to Sentinel's own ../../docker-compose.yml
# stack, this app is pointed at those same two containers. astronomy-db's init.sql still runs (it
# creates its own `astronomy_db` database, its own `astronomy_user`, inside Sentinel's Postgres
# server — a separate database, not a shared schema, so nothing here collides with Sentinel's own
# `sentinel` database and its ops_knowledge/langfuse tables); Valkey is namespaced onto Redis
# logical DB 1, since Sentinel's own cache (sentinel/core/cache.py, `redis_url` in .env) uses DB 0
# with no key prefix of its own. Run `cd ../.. && make up` before this app's `docker compose up`.
POSTGRES_HOST=postgres
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=sentinel
VALKEY_ADDR=redis:6379,defaultDatabase=1

# To use a real OpenAI API-compatible LLM,
# set the appropriate values for the target LLM
# Required permissions:
# [Models and Model capabilities]
#
# Reusing Sentinel's already-configured Google key (see ../../.env — LLM_PROVIDER=google) rather
# than provisioning a second paid API key for this app's own agent/chatbot stack (compose.agent.yaml).
# LLM_BASE_URL is the Gemini OpenAI-compatibility endpoint, so this app's LLM_BASE_URL/API_KEY
# shape (built for an OpenAI-compatible base URL) works unmodified against the same account.
#
# API_KEY is deliberately NOT set here: a plain .env value can't reference another file's
# variable (${GOOGLE_API_KEY} below would be taken literally, not substituted), and copying the
# secret into a second file means two places to rotate it. Export it into the real environment
# before `docker compose up` instead — a shell-exported var overrides a .env-file value in
# Compose. From the sentinel-rag repo root: `make otel-demo-up` does this for you; see that
# target in ../../Makefile for the one-liner if you want to run `docker compose` here directly.
LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
LLM_MODEL=gemini/gemini-2.0-flash
